{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-20118","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-21140","text":"The Three-Protocol Stack: [&], PULSE, PRISM"}]},{"id":"blk-20119","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21141","text":"This document explains how the three [&] ecosystem protocols compose into a complete substrate for accountable, evolvable, benchmarkable agent systems."}]},{"id":"blk-20120","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  PRISM    — measures loops over time      (diagnostic)   │ OS-009\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  PULSE    — declares loops + circulation   (temporal)    │ OS-010\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  [&]      — composes capabilities          (structural)  │ AmpersandBoxDesign\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"},{"id":"blk-20121","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-21142","text":"What each layer answers"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-20123","spans":[{"id":"spn-21143","text":"Layer"}]},{"id":"blk-20124","spans":[{"id":"spn-21144","text":"Question"}]},{"id":"blk-20125","spans":[{"id":"spn-21145","text":"Artifact"}]}],"id":"blk-20122","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-20126","spans":[{"id":"spn-21146","text":"[[&]](../../AmpersandBoxDesign/docs/index.md)"}]},{"id":"blk-20127","spans":[{"id":"spn-21147","text":"What can each agent do, and how do they compose?"}]},{"id":"blk-20128","spans":[{"id":"spn-21148","marks":["code"],"text":"*.ampersand.json"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20129","spans":[{"id":"spn-21149","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/spec/OS-010-PULSE-SPECIFICATION.md"}],"text":"PULSE"}]},{"id":"blk-20130","spans":[{"id":"spn-21150","text":"How do their processes cycle and signal each other?"}]},{"id":"blk-20131","spans":[{"id":"spn-21151","marks":["code"],"text":"*.pulse.json"},{"id":"spn-21152","text":" (loop manifest)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20132","spans":[{"id":"spn-21153","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/spec/OS-009-PRISM-SPECIFICATION.md"}],"text":"PRISM"}]},{"id":"blk-20133","spans":[{"id":"spn-21154","text":"How well do those cycles actually work over time?"}]},{"id":"blk-20134","spans":[{"id":"spn-21155","text":"Diagnostic reports + leaderboards"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-20135","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21156","text":"A customer adopting all three writes (at minimum) two files:"}]},{"id":"blk-20136","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"acme-insurance/\n├── acme.ampersand.json   # [&] — capability declarations\n└── acme.pulse.json       # PULSE — loop topology + cadence + connections"},{"id":"blk-20137","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21157","text":"PRISM does not require a separate file — it reads the PULSE manifest directly to discover phases, signatures, and substrates."}]},{"id":"blk-20138","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-21158","text":"Three closed loops, three nesting levels"}]},{"id":"blk-20139","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21159","text":"The reference [&] ecosystem already operates with three nested loops:"}]},{"id":"blk-20140","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"PRISM (outer)        compose → interact → observe → reflect → diagnose\n  │\n  └─ Graphonomous    retrieve → route → act → learn → consolidate\n       │\n       └─ Deliberation    survey → triage → dispatch → act → learn"},{"id":"blk-20141","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21160","text":"PULSE encodes this nesting in the "},{"id":"spn-21161","marks":["code"],"text":"nesting"},{"id":"spn-21162","text":" block of each manifest:"}]},{"id":"blk-20142","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-20144","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21163","marks":["code"],"text":"prism.benchmark"},{"id":"spn-21164","text":" declares "},{"id":"spn-21165","marks":["code"],"text":"inner_loops: [graphonomous.continual_learning]"}]}],"id":"blk-20143","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-20146","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21166","marks":["code"],"text":"graphonomous.continual_learning"},{"id":"spn-21167","text":" declares "},{"id":"spn-21168","marks":["code"],"text":"inner_loops: [graphonomous.deliberate]"}]}],"id":"blk-20145","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-20148","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21169","marks":["code"],"text":"graphonomous.deliberate"},{"id":"spn-21170","text":" declares "},{"id":"spn-21171","marks":["code"],"text":"parent_loop: graphonomous.continual_learning"}]}],"id":"blk-20147","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-20149","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21172","text":"OS-008 (Agent Harness, draft) is expected to add a fourth outer layer. PULSE supports unbounded nesting depth — adding OS-008 is just another manifest with "},{"id":"spn-21173","marks":["code"],"text":"inner_loops: [prism.benchmark]"},{"id":"spn-21174","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-20150","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-21175","text":"How signals flow"}]},{"id":"blk-20151","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21176","text":"Cross-loop signals carry one of five canonical tokens through CloudEvents-compatible envelopes:"}]},{"id":"blk-20152","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"                              ┌────────────────────┐\n                              │  ReputationUpdate  │ ────────────────┐\n                              └────────────────────┘                  │\n                                       ▲                              ▼\n                                       │                    ┌──────────────────┐\n                              ┌────────┴────────┐           │ fleetprompt.trust │\n                              │ OutcomeSignal   │           │  (marketplace)    │\n                              └────────┬────────┘           └──────────────────┘\n                                       │\n        ┌──────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────┐\n        │                              │                            │\n        ▼                              ▼                            ▼\n┌──────────────┐            ┌──────────────────┐         ┌────────────────────┐\n│ graphonomous │ ──signal──▶│  prism.benchmark │         │ agentromatic.delib │\n│ (memory loop)│            │ (eval loop)      │         │ (consensus loop)   │\n└──────┬───────┘            └────────┬─────────┘         └─────────┬──────────┘\n       │                             │                              │\n       │ TopologyContext             │ DeliberationResult           │\n       ▼                             ▼                              ▼\n┌──────────────┐            ┌──────────────────┐         ┌────────────────────┐\n│ ConsolidationEvent          (read by other loops as substrate state)        │\n└──────────────┘            └──────────────────┘         └────────────────────┘"},{"id":"blk-20153","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21177","text":"The five tokens are stable for v0.1:"}]},{"id":"blk-20154","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21178","text":"1. "},{"id":"spn-21179","marks":["code"],"text":"TopologyContext"},{"id":"spn-21180","text":" — emitted by "},{"id":"spn-21181","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve"},{"id":"spn-21182","text":", consumed by "},{"id":"spn-21183","marks":["code"],"text":"route"},{"id":"spn-21184","text":" 2. "},{"id":"spn-21185","marks":["code"],"text":"DeliberationResult"},{"id":"spn-21186","text":" — emitted by inner deliberation loops 3. "},{"id":"spn-21187","marks":["code"],"text":"OutcomeSignal"},{"id":"spn-21188","text":" — emitted by "},{"id":"spn-21189","marks":["code"],"text":"learn"},{"id":"spn-21190","text":" after action results 4. "},{"id":"spn-21191","marks":["code"],"text":"ReputationUpdate"},{"id":"spn-21192","text":" — canonical reputation/confidence delta 5. "},{"id":"spn-21193","marks":["code"],"text":"ConsolidationEvent"},{"id":"spn-21194","text":" — emitted by "},{"id":"spn-21195","marks":["code"],"text":"consolidate"},{"id":"spn-21196","text":" phases"}]},{"id":"blk-20155","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-21197","text":"Conformance composition"}]},{"id":"blk-20156","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21198","text":"A loop is "},{"id":"spn-21199","marks":["bold"],"text":"PULSE-conforming"},{"id":"spn-21200","text":" if its manifest validates against "},{"id":"spn-21201","marks":["code"],"text":"pulse-loop-manifest.v0.1.json"},{"id":"spn-21202","text":" and its runtime passes all 12 conformance tests."}]},{"id":"blk-20157","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21203","text":"A system is "},{"id":"spn-21204","marks":["bold"],"text":"PRISM-evaluable"},{"id":"spn-21205","text":" automatically once it is PULSE-conforming — PRISM's "},{"id":"spn-21206","marks":["code"],"text":"compose"},{"id":"spn-21207","text":" phase reads the manifest, injects scenarios at the declared "},{"id":"spn-21208","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve"},{"id":"spn-21209","text":" boundary, and observes outcomes via the declared "},{"id":"spn-21210","marks":["code"],"text":"learn"},{"id":"spn-21211","text":" phase."}]},{"id":"blk-20158","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21212","text":"A system is "},{"id":"spn-21213","marks":["bold"],"text":"[&]-composable"},{"id":"spn-21214","text":" if its agents declare capabilities with matching "},{"id":"spn-21215","marks":["code"],"text":"accepts_from"},{"id":"spn-21216","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-21217","marks":["code"],"text":"feeds_into"},{"id":"spn-21218","text":" contracts."}]},{"id":"blk-20159","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21219","text":"The three layers are independent. A system may adopt one without the others. Adoption order is typically:"}]},{"id":"blk-20160","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21220","text":"1. "},{"id":"spn-21221","marks":["bold"],"text":"[&]"},{"id":"spn-21222","text":" (capability declarations) — earliest, lowest commitment 2. "},{"id":"spn-21223","marks":["bold"],"text":"PULSE"},{"id":"spn-21224","text":" (loop manifest) — when the system has closed feedback 3. "},{"id":"spn-21225","marks":["bold"],"text":"PRISM"},{"id":"spn-21226","text":" (benchmarking) — when the loop is ready to be measured"}]},{"id":"blk-20161","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-21227","text":"Why three protocols, not one"}]},{"id":"blk-20162","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21228","text":"A monolithic protocol covering capabilities, loops, and benchmarking would be larger, harder to evolve, and harder to adopt incrementally. The three-layer split mirrors how HTTP, HTML, and CSS became ubiquitous separately before converging in the browser."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-20164","spans":[{"id":"spn-21229","text":"Concern"}]},{"id":"blk-20165","spans":[{"id":"spn-21230","text":"Layer"}]},{"id":"blk-20166","spans":[{"id":"spn-21231","text":"Cadence of change"}]}],"id":"blk-20163","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-20167","spans":[{"id":"spn-21232","text":"What can be done"}]},{"id":"blk-20168","spans":[{"id":"spn-21233","text":"[&]"}]},{"id":"blk-20169","spans":[{"id":"spn-21234","text":"months–years"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20170","spans":[{"id":"spn-21235","text":"How it cycles"}]},{"id":"blk-20171","spans":[{"id":"spn-21236","text":"PULSE"}]},{"id":"blk-20172","spans":[{"id":"spn-21237","text":"weeks–months"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20173","spans":[{"id":"spn-21238","text":"How well it works"}]},{"id":"blk-20174","spans":[{"id":"spn-21239","text":"PRISM"}]},{"id":"blk-20175","spans":[{"id":"spn-21240","text":"continuous"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-20176","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21241","text":"Different rates of change deserve different protocols."}]},{"id":"blk-20177","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-21242","text":"Related"}]},{"id":"blk-20178","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-20180","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21243","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/ECOSYSTEM.md"}],"text":"Ecosystem overview"},{"id":"spn-21244","text":" — how every product fits the stack"}]}],"id":"blk-20179","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-20182","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21245","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/STACK_COMPLETION.md"}],"text":"Stack status"},{"id":"spn-21246","text":" — versions, test counts, deployment state"}]}],"id":"blk-20181","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-20184","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21247","text":"[[&] Protocol docs](../../AmpersandBoxDesign/docs/index.md) — capability composition (structural)"}]}],"id":"blk-20183","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-20186","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21248","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/spec/OS-010-PULSE-SPECIFICATION.md"}],"text":"OS-010 PULSE specification"},{"id":"spn-21249","text":" — loop + circulation algebra (temporal)"}]}],"id":"blk-20185","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-20188","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21250","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/spec/OS-009-PRISM-SPECIFICATION.md"}],"text":"OS-009 PRISM specification"},{"id":"spn-21251","text":" — cross-system benchmark (diagnostic)"}]}],"id":"blk-20187","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-20190","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21252","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/graphonomous/docs/spec/README.md"}],"text":"Graphonomous spec"},{"id":"spn-21253","text":" — the reference memory loop these protocols compose around"}]}],"id":"blk-20189","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-20191","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-21254","text":"PULSE implementation docs"}]},{"id":"blk-20192","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-20194","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21255","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/PULSE/docs/ARITHMETIC_INTEGRATION.md"}],"text":"Arithmetic Integration"},{"id":"spn-21256","text":" — how PULSE phases gate on the box-and-box kernel verdict"}]}],"id":"blk-20193","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-20196","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21257","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/PULSE/docs/V0.2-BEHAVIORAL-TYPES.md"}],"text":"V0.2 Behavioral Types"},{"id":"spn-21258","text":" — session-typed phase contracts (draft)"}]}],"id":"blk-20195","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-20198","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21259","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/PULSE/docs/V0.2-IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md"}],"text":"V0.2 Implementation Plan"},{"id":"spn-21260","text":" — roadmap for the v0.2 manifest schema"}]}],"id":"blk-20197","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-20200","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21261","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/PULSE/docs/NPM_PACKAGE.md"}],"text":"NPM Package"},{"id":"spn-21262","text":" — the PULSE validator/conformance package"}]}],"id":"blk-20199","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierawdldzvol4kpmawpoo7uxsmx6taqaseagxdy3dnjumsrbcmsbkejq","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}